edia)","dt":"c. 1108","h":16,"osm":"way/235062319","kind":"church","listEntry":1247622,"listUrl":"https://historicengland.org.uk/listing/the-list/list-entry/1247622","qid":"Q7245489","image":"http://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/St%20Anthonys%20Priory%20Church%2C%20Lenton.jpg","article":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Priory_Church_of_St_Anthony,_Lenton","cat":"St Anthony's Church, Lenton","stories":[{"layer":"lenton","text":"Henry II gave Lenton Priory an eight-day fair for St Martin's Day, which Henry III lengthened to twelve, with tolls paid to the monks for every booth. The fair outlived the priory: in 1584, when servants of Mary, Queen of Scots came, it was a horse fair, and by the 17th century it was known as a great fair for all sorts of horses. In the 19th century farmers and horse dealers still came.","source":{"title":"Lenton Priory","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lenton_Priory","kind":"Wikipedia"},"when":"1584","whenSrc":{"title":"Lenton Priory","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lenton_Priory","kind":"Wikipedia"},"nm":"Lenton Fair"},{"layer":"lenton","text":"William Peverel founded a priory of Cluniac monks at Lenton in about 1102–08, and richly endowed it. In February 1538 its last prior, Nicholas Heath, and many of his monks were thrown into prison, accused of high treason. The prior, eight monks and four Lenton labourers were executed, in Nottingham and in front of the priory, and the priory was dissolved that year. Little is left: the Priory Church of St Anthony is thought to keep part of its hospital chapel.","source":{"title":"Lenton Priory","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lenton_Priory","kind":"Wikipedia"},"when":"1538","whenSrc":{"title":"Lenton Priory","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lenton_Priory","kind":"Wikipedia"},"nm":"Lenton Priory"},{"layer":"scheduled","tpl":"scheduled","of":"Lenton Priory"}],"sum":"The Priory Church of St Anthony, Lenton, also known as The Priory, is a parish church in the Church of England in Lenton, Nottingham.","sumSrc":{"title":"Priory Church of St Anthony, Lenton","kind":"Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Priory_Church_of_St_Anthony%2C_Lenton"},"council":"Nottingham City Council","xy":[-1.17876,52.94377]},"67477":{"where":"33 Gregory Street","h":8,"osm":"way/235062364","kind":"house","council":"Nottingham City Council","xy":[-1.17792,52.94409]},"67478":{"where":"35 Gregory Street","h":8,"osm":"way/235062349","kind":"house","council":"Nottingham City Council","xy":[-1.17784,52.94409]},"67479":{"where":"37 Gregory Street","h":8,"osm":"way/235062333","kind":"house","council":"Nottingham City Council","xy":[-1.17777,52.94409]},"67480":{"where":"3 and 4 Friary Close","h":8,"osm":"way/235223996","kind":"residential","council":"Nottingham City Council","xy":[-1.17799,52.94376]},"67481":{"where":"1 and 2 Friary Close","h":8,"osm":"way/235223960","kind":"residential","council":"Nottingham City Council","xy":[-1.17787,52.94374]},"67482":{"where":"5 and 6 Friary Close","h":8,"osm":"way/61774120","kind":"residential","council":"Nottingham City Council","xy":[-1.17808,52.94372]},"67483":{"where":"7 and 8 Friary Close","h":8,"osm":"way/235224009","kind":"residential","council":"Nottingham City Council","xy":[-1.17812,52.94364]},"67484":{"where":"9 and 10 Friary Close","h":8,"osm":"way/235224016","kind":"residential","council":"Nottingham City Council","xy":[-1.17817,52.94343]},"67485":{"where":"11 and 12 Friary Close","h":8,"osm":"way/61774127","kind":"residential","council":"Nottingham City Council","xy":[-1.17807,52.94341]},"67486":{"where":"13 and 14 Friary Close","h":8,"osm":"way/235223946","kind":"residential","council":"Nottingham City Council","xy":[-1.17794,52.94343]},"67487":{"where":"15 and 16 Friary Close","h":8,"osm":"way/235223950","kind":"residential","council":"Nottingham City Council","xy":[-1.17784,52.94347]},"67488":{"where":"17 and 18 Friary Close","h":8,"osm":"way/235223954","kind":"residential","council":"Nottingham City Cou